With -W interactive, every input line longer than BUFFSZ grows the input
buffer by another chunk (up to 256 KiB each time), even when the buffer
already has room, and the space is never reused. Reading ~10000 lines of
~10 KB each takes gigabytes: on 32-bit hosts mawk dies with "out of memory"
(upstream's own test/longline.sh), on 64-bit it is merely wasteful. Grow only
when the next fgets chunk would not fit. Still present in upstream's fin.c
1.62 (20241214); upstream shrank the test instead (20240825).

--- a/fin.c
+++ b/fin.c
@@ -226,7 +226,8 @@
 			 */
 			size_t my_size = (size_t) (p - fin->buff);
 
-			enlarge_fin_buffer(fin);
+			if (my_size + BUFFSZ + 1 > fin->buff_size)
+			    enlarge_fin_buffer(fin);
 			p = my_buff = my_size + fin->buff;
 			got_any = 1;
 		    }
